<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (i < index || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i))) && (\old(this.get(i)) == null => this.get(i) == null);</code>

This assert statement captures the requirement that for every index `i` from 0 to the initial size of the list (exclusive), the element at `i` either remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was null before, provided `i` is less than the insertion index.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); i < index => this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (i < index || \old(this.get(i)) == null) => this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>

Explanation:
- The comment specifies that for every index `i` from `0` to `index-1`, the element at `i` either remains unchanged or continues to be `null` if it was `null` before.
- We use `\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size());` to iterate over all indices from `0` to the initial size of the list minus one.
- The condition `(i < index || \old(this.get(i)) == null) => this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i))` ensures that if `i` is less than the insertion `index` or the element at `i` was `null` before, it remains unchanged after the insertion.
--------------------
